{#
mail/_send_outcome.stream.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
What the browser is told once the send has actually happened.

Rendered by App\Service\Mail\SendOutcomeNotifier in the WORKER, published over
Mercure, and applied by core--mercure. Rendered rather than described because
the alternative is building a toast in JavaScript, which means a second copy of
_toast.html.twig that drifts from the first.

WHY THIS EXISTS AT ALL

"Message sent." used to be said by ComposeController::sent(), which the browser
calls when the cancel window closes — at eight seconds. The send is held for
ten. So the confirmation preceded the attempt by two seconds, every time, for
everybody, and a send that then failed was never mentioned again.

Variables: message, sent (bool)
#}
<turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
            type:    sent ? 'success' : 'error',
            message: sent
                ? 'toast.sent'|trans
                : 'toast.send_failed'|trans({ '%subject%': message.subject|default('')|slice(0, 60) }),
            extra:   sent ? {} : { hide_after: 12000 },
        } only %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
